    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28850" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mesauloe</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ), ōn, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέσαυλοι</span>.—In archit.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>narrow passages
				between two rooms</i> or <i>walls</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter duo autem peristylia itinera sunt, quae
					mesauloe dicuntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 6,
					7</span></i>
			 (10), 5; cf. andron.</div>
